{"id":"3df92301c973942b57d4ee6a63f1966d2cdd65fe","axis":"silent","repo":"strapi/strapi","sha":"3df92301c973942b57d4ee6a63f1966d2cdd65fe","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/docs/packages/core/utils/index.md","lines":["@@ -37,6 +37,20 @@ An app can load two copies of `@strapi/utils` when its Strapi packages are on di"," "," `traverseEntity` walks a data entity along its schema. It calls a `Visitor` for each attribute, and it recurses into relations, media, components and dynamic zones. The `traverse` namespace does the same for query parameters: fields, filters, sort and populate. See [traverseEntity](./traverse-entity.md)."," ","+`traverseQueryPopulate` recurses into relations, media, components, `on` fragments of dynamic zones and polymorphic relations, and nested `populate` keys. It does not recurse into `sort`, `filters` and `fields` keys. A visitor that checks them runs the matching traversal itself, as the default validators and sanitizers do. A visitor must not recurse into a nested `populate`, because the traversal already visits it with the same visitor.","+","+Below a relation, media, component or `on` fragment, the keys of a populate value are query keywords, even when the schema also has an attribute with the same name. There, `populate` is always a nested populate of that schema, and `sort`, `filters` and `fields` are not walked. Elsewhere, a key that names an attribute is that attribute.","+","+#### Writing a populate visitor","+","+`traverseQueryPopulate` deep-copies the populate it is given once, before it walks it. The levels below are not copied again, and neither is a value a visitor sets. A custom visitor follows three rules:","+","+- Change the populate only with `set` and `remove`.","+- Never write into `value` or `data`. Build a new object or array and `set` it.","+- `set` a fresh value, not one that is shared with anything else, such as a module constant or the query of the caller.","+","+Earlier versions deep-copied every level, so a visitor that wrote into its `value` changed only the copy of that level. Now the write reaches the one copy that every later level and visitor reads. If a visitor sets a shared value, a later write also reaches the other owners of that value. [`populate-copy.vitest.test.ts`](https://github.com/strapi/strapi/blob/develop/packages/core/utils/src/__tests__/populate-copy.vitest.test.ts) runs each built-in populate visitor with the values it is handed frozen.","+"," ### Sanitize and validate"," "," `sanitize.createAPISanitizers` and `validate.createAPIValidators` build the Content API input, output and query checks from `traverseEntity` visitors. The `sanitize` visitors (`remove-*`) drop what is not allowed. The `validate` visitors (`throw-*`) throw a `ValidationError` instead. `@strapi/core` creates both in its `content-api` service."],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/core/utils/src/__tests__/__snapshots__/populate-corpus.vitest.test.ts.snap","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,2965 @@","+// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html","+","+exports[`populate validation and sanitization corpus > boolean object 1`] = `","+{","+  \"documentServiceValidate\": {","+    \"passes\": \"unchanged\",","+  },","+  \"queryLayer\": \"e54ee28fc042\",","+  \"sanitized\": \"unchanged\",","+  \"sanitizedWithoutAuth\": \"same as with auth\",","+  \"validate\": \"passes\",","+}","+`;","+","+exports[`populate validation and sanitization corpus > chain depth 1 1`] = `","+{","+  \"documentServiceValidate\": {","+    \"passes\": \"unchanged\",","+  },","+  \"queryLayer\": \"036108a3ef96\",","+  \"sanitized\": \"unchanged\",","+  \"sanitizedWithoutAuth\": \"same as with auth\",","+  \"validate\": \"passes\",","+}","+`;","+","+exports[`populate validation and sanitization corpus > chain depth 1 ending in a dot string 1`] = `","+{","+  \"documentServiceValidate\": {","+    \"passes\": \"unchanged\",","+  },","+  \"queryLayer\": \"f957800d2b2e\",","+  \"sanitized\": \"uncha